Particle Rain's own files used by the port, from
src/main/resources/assets/particlerain/ (MIT):
- textures/particle/*.png (in mixins/particlerain/textures.rs, made by
  tools/generate.mjs), the icon (mixins/particlerain/data/icon.png) and the
  weather sounds sounds/weather/*.ogg (mixins/particlerain/data/);
- particles.json, its built-in particles (mixins/particlerain/defaults.rs);
- lang/en_us.json and lang/ru_ru.json (mixins/particlerain/lang.rs). Where
  the original's Russian file has no line, the port has its own Russian
  (tools/assets/ru_port.json).

As in the original, the rain and snow sprites are cut from the game's own
rain and snow textures (or a resource pack's) and the ripples are drawn when
the textures load.

Horizon has no `c:` convention tags (Fabric API defines them in Java). The
port defines the ones Particle Rain's built-in particles name
(c:in_overworld, c:is_wet, c:climate_wet, c:is_spooky, c:is_windswept,
c:sandstone_blocks, c:glass_panes) after Fabric API's conventional tags.

Port addition (not in the original): the "Changing Wind Direction" wind option
(config key horizonChangingWindDirection, on by default) turns the original's
north-west wind slowly with the game time; off is exactly the original.

This port rewrites Particle Rain's weather particles, spawning, wind, sounds,
settings and config screens in Rust for Horizon's native mod API. It is not
affiliated with PigCart, Mojang or Microsoft.
